### ==============================================================================
### DecisionHub Backend API Test Suite
### Compatible with VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 1. HEALTH CHECKS & SYSTEM STATUS
### ==============================================================================

### 1.1 Root Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/ HTTP/1.1

### 1.2 Health Check (v1 API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health HTTP/1.1

### 1.3 Health Check (Legacy Path)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health HTTP/1.1



### ==============================================================================
### 2. AUTHENTICATION & USER MANAGEMENT
### ==============================================================================

### 2.1 Register New User - Success
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Johnson",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.2 Register User - Duplicate Email (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "Alice Duplicate",
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2.3 Register User - Validation Error (Invalid Email & Short Password)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/register HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "fullName": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 2.4 Login User - Success (Captures JWT token for subsequent requests)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### Store the JWT token from login response
@authToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJhbGljZUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTc5NDcyNDczNCwiZXhwIjoxNzk0ODExMTM0fQ.eEWPIM1AxO2xB3mIIqJVu5Ur71zj1EoV6-2rOoJCp74

### 2.5 Login User - Incorrect Password (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "alice@example.com",
  "password": "WrongPassword!"
}

### 2.6 Login User - Unknown Email (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "nonexistent.user@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}


### ==============================================================================
### 3. PROTECTED ENDPOINTS & AUTHORIZATION CHECKS
### ==============================================================================

### 3.1 Protected Endpoint Without Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1

### 3.2 Protected Endpoint With Invalid Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer invalid-or-tampered-token-12345

### 3.3 Protected Endpoint With Valid Bearer Token (Passes Security Filter)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}



### ==============================================================================
### 4. DECISION BOARD MANAGEMENT (MILESTONE 2 - PHASE 1)
### ==============================================================================

### 4.1 Create Decision - Success (PUBLIC with initial options)
# @name createDecision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Select Core Backend Architecture",
  "description": "Choose between Monolith vs Microservices for high scale deployment.",
  "category": "Technology",
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "status": "ACTIVE",
  "pollType": "SINGLE_CHOICE",
  "options": [
    {
      "title": "Modular Monolith",
      "description": "High cohesion, single deployment unit, easy refactoring",
      "displayOrder": 0
    },
    {
      "title": "Microservices",
      "description": "Independently deployable bounded contexts with event bus",
      "displayOrder": 1
    }
  ]
}

### Store the created decision ID
@decisionId = {{createDecision.response.body.data.id}}

### 4.2 Create Decision - Validation Failure (Blank fields, Expected: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": ""
}

### 4.3 Create Decision - Unauthenticated (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "title": "Unauthorized Decision",
  "description": "Should be rejected without valid token",
  "category": "Security"
}

### 4.4 Retrieve Public Decisions (Paginated, Public Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/public?page=0&size=10&sortBy=createdAt&sortDir=desc HTTP/1.1

### 4.5 Retrieve Decisions (Authenticated Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions?page=0&size=10 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.6 Retrieve Decisions Created by Authenticated User
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/my?page=0&size=10 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.7 Retrieve Decision by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.8 Retrieve Decision by Missing ID (Expected: 404 Not Found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/999999 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4.9 Update Decision (Creator or Admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Select Core Backend Architecture (Updated)",
  "description": "Updated context with deployment metrics and cost analysis.",
  "category": "Technology",
  "visibility": "PUBLIC",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 4.10 Delete Decision (Creator or Admin)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}} HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}


### ==============================================================================
### 5. OPTION MANAGEMENT
### ==============================================================================

### 5.1 Add Multiple Options to Decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "options": [
    {
      "title": "Serverless Functions",
      "description": "Event-driven compute scaled to zero when idle",
      "displayOrder": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Edge Compute",
      "description": "Distributed edge nodes for ultra-low latency",
      "displayOrder": 3
    }
  ]
}

### 5.2 Retrieve All Options for Decision
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5.3 Update Option within Decision
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Modular Monolith (Optimized)",
  "description": "Single repository with Spring Modulith boundaries",
  "displayOrder": 0
}

### 5.4 Update Option - Cross-Decision Mismatch (Expected: 400 Bad Request)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/99999 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: {{contentType}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

{
  "title": "Option Not Belonging to Decision",
  "description": "Should fail with 400 Bad Request"
}

### 5.5 Delete Option within Decision
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/decisions/{{decisionId}}/options/1 HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
